course: dictionary
lesson: 11308
title: Yeast: a tiny living helper
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Yeast is a tiny living thing, a kind of fungus, so it is not a plant or an animal. Bakers use it to make bread rise. Look for clues in the sentence: «Warmth makes yeast work faster, so dough is left somewhere warm.» Warm places help it work, so yeast is alive and busy.
explain: Context tells you what a word does, not only what it is. «Cakes rise without yeast, using baking powder or whisked eggs to trap gas.» The clue is without: cakes can rise with other things, so yeast is one way to make dough rise, not the only way.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Try «Mushrooms, moulds and yeast are all fungi.» If yeast means a tiny living fungus, the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is probably right.
fact: Yeast is a living fungus, so it needs sugar, water and warmth to grow.
fact: In bread, «yeast» makes gas (carbon dioxide) that puffs up the dough, so it rises.
fact: Warmth makes yeast work faster; in a cold fridge the dough rises very slowly.
fact: «Matzah» is a flat bread made without yeast, eaten at Passover.
fact: «Dried yeast» and «fresh yeast» are two forms that bakers buy for baking.
exercise: «Warmth makes yeast work faster, so dough is left somewhere warm.» Why is the dough left somewhere warm? | To make the bread taste of fish | *To help the yeast work faster | To make the dough freeze solid | To stop the yeast from being alive
exercise: «Mushrooms, moulds and yeast are all fungi.» What group do mushrooms, moulds and yeast belong to? | *Fungi | Minerals | Plants | Animals
exercise: Jayden asks, «What is yeast?» What is the best answer? | A metal used in ovens | *A tiny living fungus that makes bread rise | Flour made from wheat | A kind of sugar that is always cold
test: «Cakes rise without yeast, using baking powder or whisked eggs to trap gas.» Which word tells you yeast is not the only way to make a cake rise? | cakes | *without | rise | oven
test: «Passover... matzah, a flat bread made without yeast.» Why does matzah stay flat? | Because it has too much yeast | Because it is baked in cold water | *Because it has no yeast to make gas that lifts the dough | Because it is made from fish
exam: Jayden says yeast is a mineral from the ground. What is correct? | Yeast is a kind of salt | *Yeast is a tiny living fungus, not a mineral | Yeast is a mineral that is dug out of rock | Yeast is a plant seed
